00:10:14.820 --> 00:10:17.582
we think about security
in the hybrid world.

00:10:17.582 --> 00:10:19.040
JESS ELROY: Yeah.

00:10:19.040 --> 00:10:26.080
OK, so over the course of
2019, as we look at this year,

00:10:26.080 --> 00:10:29.500
we've sort of got four
main pillars of work

00:10:29.500 --> 00:10:30.640
that we're doing.

00:10:30.640 --> 00:10:34.520
And they tie into the way that
Anthos looks at the world.

00:10:34.520 --> 00:10:37.157
So we think of security
of the cloud, which

00:10:37.157 --> 00:10:39.490
are all of the different
security controls that we built

00:10:39.490 --> 00:10:41.890
in, all the compliance and
regulatory compliance that we

00:10:41.890 --> 00:10:45.130
do, all of the
default encryption,

00:10:45.130 --> 00:10:48.012
and strong authentication
on connections.

00:10:48.012 --> 00:10:50.470
You don't have to do anything
in order to get those things.

00:10:50.470 --> 00:10:54.460
Then security in the
cloud, where we provide you

00:10:54.460 --> 00:10:56.560
with all of the
configurations and options

00:10:56.560 --> 00:11:00.310
that you create your
own security settings

00:11:00.310 --> 00:11:01.780
and portfolios from.

00:11:01.780 --> 00:11:04.540
Those are your firewall
settings, your VPC Service

00:11:04.540 --> 00:11:09.910
Controls for logical
boundaries, IM and org policies.

00:11:09.910 --> 00:11:12.070
And then security services--
so this year, you'll

00:11:12.070 --> 00:11:13.780
see new things from
us on the services

00:11:13.780 --> 00:11:16.210
side, where we are
building services

00:11:16.210 --> 00:11:18.280
on top of those things.

00:11:18.280 --> 00:11:20.980
And then our fourth goal
is around securing Anthos.

00:11:20.980 --> 00:11:23.740
So all of the work
that we're doing

00:11:23.740 --> 00:11:25.330
needs to be portable to Anthos.

00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:29.560
So we are taking the
best of GKE security,

00:11:29.560 --> 00:11:33.040
Istio security, secure
pipelines through GKE,

00:11:33.040 --> 00:11:39.100
secure connections, and Envoy
and certificates through Istio,

00:11:39.100 --> 00:11:42.730
and leveraging all of
that through Anthos.

00:11:42.730 --> 00:11:46.450
So we're securing
the platform itself,

00:11:46.450 --> 00:11:49.000
On-Prem, and as you
migrate, you get

00:11:49.000 --> 00:11:52.520
all the benefits of the other
pieces in the cloud as well.

00:11:52.520 --> 00:11:53.948
So it's a really nice fit.

00:11:53.948 --> 00:11:55.990
Those security services
that I was talking about,

00:11:55.990 --> 00:11:58.120
we'll announce a bunch
of those tomorrow.

00:11:58.120 --> 00:12:00.280
And you'll see us start
to push those down

00:12:00.280 --> 00:12:03.420
towards Anthos as well over
the course of this year.

00:12:03.420 --> 00:12:05.170
RAE WANG: That's a top
benefit for Anthos,

00:12:05.170 --> 00:12:08.838
even without moving
your workloads off-prem,

00:12:08.838 --> 00:12:11.380
you can already start to benefit
from a lot of these security

00:12:11.380 --> 00:12:13.220
value from [INAUDIBLE].

00:12:13.220 --> 00:12:14.140
Cool.

00:12:14.140 --> 00:12:16.480
Another big
announcement from Anthos

00:12:16.480 --> 00:12:18.123
this morning was
our Marketplace.

00:12:18.123 --> 00:12:19.540
So, Alberto, why
don't you tell us

00:12:19.540 --> 00:12:23.173
what it means to customers,
especially to enterprises.

00:12:23.173 --> 00:12:24.590
ALBERTO MAESTRO:
I'm super-excited

00:12:24.590 --> 00:12:27.370
about the Marketplace.

00:12:27.370 --> 00:12:33.100
The reason being is because now
that we have a platform where

00:12:33.100 --> 00:12:38.290
customers can start
investing and building

00:12:38.290 --> 00:12:43.160
their applications, they have
the need to run the existing--

00:12:43.160 --> 00:12:46.090
the way they manage
the existing solutions

00:12:46.090 --> 00:12:49.370
it was as laborious as they were
building their own platform.

00:12:49.370 --> 00:12:52.020
So we have the opportunity
to actually help

00:12:52.020 --> 00:12:56.560
our partners come
into the platform

00:12:56.560 --> 00:12:58.600
and meet their customers
on the platform,

00:12:58.600 --> 00:13:01.210
and simplify the
operational process,

00:13:01.210 --> 00:13:05.470
the procurement process, such as
all our customers can find all

00:13:05.470 --> 00:13:08.050
their applications, all
the services that they need

00:13:08.050 --> 00:13:09.970
at the click of
a button and have

00:13:09.970 --> 00:13:13.390
the whole lifecycle in ensuring
that those services are deliver

00:13:13.390 --> 00:13:14.770
in a consistent way.

00:13:14.770 --> 00:13:19.340
One of the things that customers
tell us is that, yeah, great,

00:13:19.340 --> 00:13:20.740
we love your platform.

00:13:20.740 --> 00:13:26.410
But when something goes wrong,
who do I have to talk to?

00:13:26.410 --> 00:13:28.330
So a lot of
investment is going on

00:13:28.330 --> 00:13:30.880
to make sure that there
is a consistent way

00:13:30.880 --> 00:13:34.270
to deliver and run those
services in Anthos such

00:13:34.270 --> 00:13:36.820
that our customers have
a consistent experience,

00:13:36.820 --> 00:13:42.100
and they can actually
spend more time just

00:13:42.100 --> 00:13:44.980
building their applications
versus trying to figure out

00:13:44.980 --> 00:13:47.693
what throat to choke.

00:13:47.693 --> 00:13:48.360
RAE WANG: Great.

00:13:48.360 --> 00:13:48.890
Thank you.

00:13:48.890 --> 00:13:52.050
OK, so I will wait a
little bit to come back

00:13:52.050 --> 00:13:53.130
to the Moscone questions.

00:13:53.130 --> 00:13:55.190
Let's come back to this room.

00:13:55.190 --> 00:13:59.280
We can open for live questions.

00:13:59.280 --> 00:14:00.150
Lucy has the mic.

00:14:08.770 --> 00:14:11.380
AUDIENCE: So the last
year at GCP Next, the CSD

00:14:11.380 --> 00:14:12.260
was announced, right?

00:14:12.260 --> 00:14:14.950
And as part of that,
the GKE On-Prem

00:14:14.950 --> 00:14:18.240
was part of that offering,
and then Managed Istio

00:14:18.240 --> 00:14:19.630
was one of them, right?

00:14:19.630 --> 00:14:21.190
And now, we have Anthos.

00:14:21.190 --> 00:14:24.470
So has that been a change
in strategy from last year,

00:14:24.470 --> 00:14:28.630
or is it just an extension of--

00:14:28.630 --> 00:14:31.035
APARNA SINHA: Yeah, so
no change in strategy.

00:14:34.050 --> 00:14:35.650
So the announcement
from last year,

00:14:35.650 --> 00:14:37.910
we've taken it
forward next step.

00:14:37.910 --> 00:14:42.240
GKE On-Prem, what we announced
as part of Anthos, is now GA.

00:14:42.240 --> 00:14:45.967
And we saw tremendous demand
when we announced it last year.

00:14:45.967 --> 00:14:47.550
I think we mentioned
in our spotlight,

00:14:47.550 --> 00:14:50.640
we had over 1,000
customers sign up.

00:14:50.640 --> 00:14:52.990
And so we took that
customer feedback.

00:14:52.990 --> 00:14:55.110
We actually worked directly
with those customers

00:14:55.110 --> 00:14:57.360
to bring the product
through alpha,

00:14:57.360 --> 00:15:00.450
beta, and now,
announced GA here today.

00:15:00.450 --> 00:15:01.950
What we've done,
though, in addition

00:15:01.950 --> 00:15:03.540
is we've added
several components

00:15:03.540 --> 00:15:07.140
into the overall
platform that is Anthos.

00:15:07.140 --> 00:15:11.050
Last year, we also announced the
config management capability,

00:15:11.050 --> 00:15:13.890
which is from a single
source of truth.

00:15:13.890 --> 00:15:15.570
Across all your
different environments

00:15:15.570 --> 00:15:18.150
and all your different clusters,
you can deploy policies--

00:15:18.150 --> 00:15:21.090
RBAC policies, quota policies,
a number of different policies.

00:15:21.090 --> 00:15:22.710
That also moved to GA.

00:15:22.710 --> 00:15:25.020
And last year was when we
announced the introduction

00:15:25.020 --> 00:15:26.110
of the Marketplace.

00:15:26.110 --> 00:15:28.800
And as Alberto stated,
that has also moved to GA.

00:15:28.800 --> 00:15:32.100
So those three components
very tightly moved to GA

00:15:32.100 --> 00:15:33.283
as part of Anthos.

00:15:33.283 --> 00:15:35.700
And of course, the Managed
Istio piece-- the Managed Istio

00:15:35.700 --> 00:15:39.420
piece, I think, we previously
announced that as beta in GKE.

00:15:39.420 --> 00:15:40.860
And we're moving forward.

00:15:40.860 --> 00:15:42.510
And over the course
of our roadmap

00:15:42.510 --> 00:15:46.750
this year, we'll be bringing
that to the rest of Anthos.

00:15:46.750 --> 00:15:48.250
AUDIENCE: I have
one more question

00:15:48.250 --> 00:15:49.900
about the Anthos Migrate.

00:15:49.900 --> 00:15:51.100
So that's a new thing.

00:15:51.100 --> 00:15:53.710
That was not something which
was there last year, right?

00:15:53.710 --> 00:15:56.200
And I think you
mentioned that there

00:15:56.200 --> 00:15:58.990
are some customers who are
already leveraging it or using

00:15:58.990 --> 00:15:59.650
that, right?

00:15:59.650 --> 00:16:03.130
I'm just trying to understand--

00:16:03.130 --> 00:16:05.020
because we come
from a legacy world.

00:16:05.020 --> 00:16:07.330
And we are migrating
applications to the cloud.

00:16:07.330 --> 00:16:12.160
And how easy, in that case,
wood Anthos Migrate be?

00:16:12.160 --> 00:16:14.450
Because you're dealing
with monolith application

00:16:14.450 --> 00:16:16.300
with different databases,
and then we use

00:16:16.300 --> 00:16:19.390
managed services or managed
databases in the cloud.

00:16:19.390 --> 00:16:22.750
So in that case, would
Anthos Migrate be applicable,

00:16:22.750 --> 00:16:25.300
or is it something
where you already

00:16:25.300 --> 00:16:28.510
built cloud-native applications,
and only then you can use it?

00:16:28.510 --> 00:16:31.190
APARNA SINHA: No,
actually, Anthos Migrate,

00:16:31.190 --> 00:16:34.278
it's one of two new capabilities
as part of Anthos this year.

00:16:34.278 --> 00:16:35.820
So we talked about
what moved to GA--

00:16:35.820 --> 00:16:37.945
just the three or four
capabilities we talked about

00:16:37.945 --> 00:16:38.650
last year--

00:16:38.650 --> 00:16:41.330
and the two new capabilities
that we introduced this year.

00:16:41.330 --> 00:16:46.060
One is Anthos Migrate, which
takes your existing monoliths,

00:16:46.060 --> 00:16:48.610
including your
databases, some things,

00:16:48.610 --> 00:16:54.310
like Sybase, your WebSphere.

00:16:54.310 --> 00:16:57.910
We showed a CRM
application, SugarCRM.

00:16:57.910 --> 00:17:01.420
So very much existing,
what you might call,

00:17:01.420 --> 00:17:03.520
packaged applications,
where you might not even

00:17:03.520 --> 00:17:06.910
have the source code, that's
what Anthos Migrate targets.

00:17:06.910 --> 00:17:11.650
And it moves that as a
system container into GKE.

00:17:11.650 --> 00:17:13.680
And we announced that
that capability--

00:17:13.680 --> 00:17:14.638
It's brand new.

00:17:14.638 --> 00:17:16.180
It's something that,
I think, is kind

00:17:16.180 --> 00:17:17.980
of a first in the
industry, particularly

00:17:17.980 --> 00:17:20.410
given the speed and the
simplicity of the migration.

00:17:20.410 --> 00:17:22.630
So we showed a demo
in our spotlight,

00:17:22.630 --> 00:17:24.520
where it was less
than five minutes.

00:17:24.520 --> 00:17:27.310
Of course, we were
biting our nails.

00:17:27.310 --> 00:17:32.530
But we did the migration
right there on the stage.

00:17:32.530 --> 00:17:34.450
Kicked it off, and
then completed it

00:17:34.450 --> 00:17:36.670
right there on the
stage in five minutes

00:17:36.670 --> 00:17:38.740
into a system
container, bringing you

00:17:38.740 --> 00:17:42.100
the benefits of the bin packing,
the benefits of the isolation

00:17:42.100 --> 00:17:44.710
from the OS
patching, and freedom

00:17:44.710 --> 00:17:47.170
from the VM and, of
course, bringing you

00:17:47.170 --> 00:17:50.440
into a tool chain, where you
have Managed Istio enabled

00:17:50.440 --> 00:17:51.670
in that GKE environment.

00:17:51.670 --> 00:17:54.700
So you can view
that CRM system now.

00:17:54.700 --> 00:17:59.890
Still a monolith as a service
in Stackdriver and so forth

00:17:59.890 --> 00:18:01.130
and set security policy.

00:18:01.130 --> 00:18:03.130
So it brings it into
the Anthos framework.

00:18:03.130 --> 00:18:05.140
That's why it's
called Anthos Migrate.

00:18:05.140 --> 00:18:07.390
And yet, we do that
with zero code changes,

00:18:07.390 --> 00:18:09.850
so not breaking the monolith.

00:18:09.850 --> 00:18:12.205
But I do want to say
that's the first step.

00:18:12.205 --> 00:18:13.330
That's just the first step.

00:18:13.330 --> 00:18:15.190
You may want to break
the monolith, ultimately.

00:18:15.190 --> 00:18:17.523
Certainly, the customers that
I have that are on Sybase,

00:18:17.523 --> 00:18:20.320
they don't intend to
be Sybase forever.

00:18:20.320 --> 00:18:21.880
They are thinking
of breaking it.

00:18:21.880 --> 00:18:24.580
But this is a good first step.

00:18:24.580 --> 00:18:27.370
How easy is it to do?

00:18:27.370 --> 00:18:31.030
It's not that difficult. It's
actually surprisingly easy.

00:18:31.030 --> 00:18:34.150
It's based on and built on using
the same technology that you'd

00:18:34.150 --> 00:18:37.230
used for VM-to-VM
migration, which

00:18:37.230 --> 00:18:39.230
we acquired through a
company called Velostrata.

00:18:39.230 --> 00:18:42.550
And so it's actually
fairly enterprise-ready

00:18:42.550 --> 00:18:43.810
But there is setup involved.

00:18:43.810 --> 00:18:48.220
You have to set up the agent
in your vSphere environment.

00:18:48.220 --> 00:18:50.260
But it's actually
quite rich, and we've

00:18:50.260 --> 00:18:53.200
got a handful of customers
that are doing this already.

00:18:53.200 --> 00:18:55.870
We mentioned Cardinal Health.

00:18:55.870 --> 00:18:59.620
We actually mentioned a
couple others on stage.

00:18:59.620 --> 00:19:01.600
And it's pretty versatile.

00:19:01.600 --> 00:19:03.470
This is just the
beginning of our roadmap.

00:19:03.470 --> 00:19:05.630
So you can migrate
from VMware on-prem.

00:19:05.630 --> 00:19:07.870
You can also migrate
from VMs and AWS.

00:19:07.870 --> 00:19:10.465
And in future, the destination--

00:19:10.465 --> 00:19:12.840
right now, it's just GKE in
the cloud, but in the future,

00:19:12.840 --> 00:19:16.090
it will also be GKE On-Prem.

00:19:16.090 --> 00:19:18.150
And we'll continue adding
applications to it.

00:19:21.007 --> 00:19:22.840
CHEN GOLDBERG: I would
just like to add just

00:19:22.840 --> 00:19:23.760
to complete the picture.

00:19:23.760 --> 00:19:25.677
You asked, well, this
is a change of strategy.

00:19:25.677 --> 00:19:28.950
And we talked about what was
added this year around Anthos.

00:19:28.950 --> 00:19:30.990
So we mentioned
the Anthos Migrate.

00:19:30.990 --> 00:19:33.210
We also talked about
the multi-cloud

00:19:33.210 --> 00:19:34.630
this time for the first time.

00:19:34.630 --> 00:19:36.725
So already, last year, we
talked about connecting

00:19:36.725 --> 00:19:38.100
all your Kubernetes
environments,

00:19:38.100 --> 00:19:40.650
your GKE environments from
a single control plane,

00:19:40.650 --> 00:19:42.120
from a single pane of glass.

00:19:42.120 --> 00:19:45.240
And this year, we're talking
about connecting any Kubernetes

00:19:45.240 --> 00:19:47.430
cluster into that
environment and actually

00:19:47.430 --> 00:19:52.450
applying similar policies, and
tools, and experience on there.

00:19:52.450 --> 00:19:55.530
And the third thing-- actually,
I will add two more things--

00:19:55.530 --> 00:19:58.230
we also did the Cloud Run.

00:19:58.230 --> 00:19:59.910
So we demoed that today.

00:19:59.910 --> 00:20:03.270
So everything we do here is
about engineering velocity.

00:20:03.270 --> 00:20:06.420
They don't really
care about Kubernetes.

00:20:06.420 --> 00:20:09.570
So we are helping customers
with Cloud Run move

00:20:09.570 --> 00:20:12.360
from a container image
to a running application,

00:20:12.360 --> 00:20:15.100
internet-facing running
application in seconds.

00:20:15.100 --> 00:20:17.950
It's that easy, and
we also showed that.

00:20:17.950 --> 00:20:20.592
So that'll be the other
thing that we have added.

00:20:20.592 --> 00:20:22.300
And the last thing,
which I'm very happy,

00:20:22.300 --> 00:20:25.050
which also part of the
Marketplace and so on

00:20:25.050 --> 00:20:28.300
is really the ecosystem that
is built on top of Anthos.

00:20:28.300 --> 00:20:31.740
So TK today in his keynote
spent much of his time

00:20:31.740 --> 00:20:35.670
talking about the partnerships,
if it's hardware, software.

00:20:35.670 --> 00:20:38.160
You saw their system
integrated-- it was ISV--

00:20:38.160 --> 00:20:43.540
really having that support and
community in delivering Anthos.

00:20:43.540 --> 00:20:45.690
So that would be the complete
new things in Anthos.

00:20:45.690 --> 00:20:48.330
But this is really the
next step as we see it

00:20:48.330 --> 00:20:50.610
in the journey in modernization.

00:20:53.188 --> 00:20:53.980
AUDIENCE: Hi there.

00:20:53.980 --> 00:20:56.020
Kuna from [INAUDIBLE].

00:20:56.020 --> 00:20:58.080
So you guys touched on
a couple of things--

00:20:58.080 --> 00:21:00.820
breaking up the
monolith, multi-cloud.

00:21:00.820 --> 00:21:02.730
I had a question.

00:21:02.730 --> 00:21:05.950
I was talking to Lucy
about this earlier.

00:21:05.950 --> 00:21:07.810
The Anthos things
looks very cool,

00:21:07.810 --> 00:21:11.110
but it seems to assume that
your application runs completely

00:21:11.110 --> 00:21:13.330
and entirely inside Kubernetes.

00:21:13.330 --> 00:21:17.620
What if you tried to make
use of cloud-native services,

00:21:17.620 --> 00:21:24.830
like Pub/Sub, or even
Amazon queuing services?

00:21:24.830 --> 00:21:26.890
Do you guys have
any plans for Anthos

00:21:26.890 --> 00:21:32.480
to support things
outside of Kubernetes?

00:21:32.480 --> 00:21:34.493
I'm not sure if
that makes sense.

00:21:34.493 --> 00:21:35.660
ALBERTO MAESTRO: Absolutely.

00:21:35.660 --> 00:21:39.590
So one of the things that have
come in throughout the year,

00:21:39.590 --> 00:21:43.850
we have a very rich
roadmap of capabilities

00:21:43.850 --> 00:21:47.130
that are becoming part of
Anthos throughout the year.

00:21:47.130 --> 00:21:50.900
And we have talked
in many sessions

00:21:50.900 --> 00:21:55.490
around our Istio technology
and service mesh.

00:21:55.490 --> 00:21:58.130
And one of our
goals is making sure

00:21:58.130 --> 00:22:00.650
that whatever the
workload is running,

00:22:00.650 --> 00:22:07.080
we give you the capabilities
to manage how any workload--

00:22:07.080 --> 00:22:09.440
wherever they are and
how it is implemented--

00:22:09.440 --> 00:22:13.785
how we can actually help you
manage the data plane between

00:22:13.785 --> 00:22:17.930
the VM and the container, a VM
and a VM, a VM and a service,

00:22:17.930 --> 00:22:20.450
a container-- all
the permutations--

00:22:20.450 --> 00:22:23.810
effectively gives you
the same policy system

00:22:23.810 --> 00:22:27.410
that we are implementing
today to manage effectively

00:22:27.410 --> 00:22:28.940
containerized workloads.

00:22:28.940 --> 00:22:31.460
We will give you the same
capabilities to manage the data

00:22:31.460 --> 00:22:35.282
plane and, therefore, connecting
and modernizing the way all

00:22:35.282 --> 00:22:36.740
applications that
you are running--

00:22:36.740 --> 00:22:38.782
whatever they are running,
however they have been

00:22:38.782 --> 00:22:40.130
implemented--

00:22:40.130 --> 00:22:41.830
we'll give you
those capabilities.

00:22:41.830 --> 00:22:45.330
So that's one of the
investments that we are doing.

00:22:45.330 --> 00:22:48.248
And we will shape it
throughout the year.

00:22:48.248 --> 00:22:50.290
Is there anything else
that you guys want to add?

00:22:54.050 --> 00:22:54.550
Great.

00:22:54.550 --> 00:23:02.080
So there's many levels of how we
are enabling managed services.

00:23:02.080 --> 00:23:04.780
One of the principles that
we are applying to Anthos

00:23:04.780 --> 00:23:06.790
is that when we think
about the services

00:23:06.790 --> 00:23:08.860
that we bring into
Anthos is that we're

00:23:08.860 --> 00:23:11.850
going to treat first party and
third-party services the same.

00:23:11.850 --> 00:23:14.627
We want to give you exactly
the same consistency

00:23:14.627 --> 00:23:16.210
that we are bringing
into the platform

00:23:16.210 --> 00:23:17.518
with first-party services.

00:23:17.518 --> 00:23:19.060
We want to bring
the same consistency

00:23:19.060 --> 00:23:20.060
to third-party services.

00:23:22.700 --> 00:23:25.420
Our goal is to make sure
that whatever services

00:23:25.420 --> 00:23:27.880
that we bring into Anthos
work everywhere where

00:23:27.880 --> 00:23:29.830
you want Anthos to run.

00:23:29.830 --> 00:23:35.330
That is one of our goals,
and the journey just started.

00:23:35.330 --> 00:23:40.360
One of the things that we are
announcing throughout Next

00:23:40.360 --> 00:23:43.690
is the Kubernetes Marketplace
and all the partners

00:23:43.690 --> 00:23:46.000
that we have in the Kubernetes
Marketplace, but also,

00:23:46.000 --> 00:23:47.920
some things that are
truly [INAUDIBLE]..

00:23:47.920 --> 00:23:50.920
For example, Palo Alto
Networks have actually

00:23:50.920 --> 00:23:52.990
shaped as part of the
Kubernetes Marketplace

00:23:52.990 --> 00:23:57.190
the capability of integrating
the threat detection appliance

00:23:57.190 --> 00:23:58.640
with one click of a button.

00:23:58.640 --> 00:24:00.250
So you have a
Kubernetes environment.

00:24:00.250 --> 00:24:03.270
You deploy this adapter.

00:24:03.270 --> 00:24:05.620
And that connects your
threat detection appliance

00:24:05.620 --> 00:24:09.820
to your Anthos
service mesh, such

00:24:09.820 --> 00:24:11.500
as you get all of
that capability

00:24:11.500 --> 00:24:13.400
without having to
change any code.

00:24:13.400 --> 00:24:15.850
And we'll see that there
is a lot of services

00:24:15.850 --> 00:24:19.930
that we are going to
bring into Anthos that

00:24:19.930 --> 00:24:24.550
are going to give you all the
capabilities that you need

00:24:24.550 --> 00:24:27.110
to be able, not just to
modernize your application,

00:24:27.110 --> 00:24:29.388
but also integrate with
existing applications.

00:24:32.510 --> 00:24:35.570
AUDIENCE: Maybe a related
question to that as well.

00:24:35.570 --> 00:24:37.310
